    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2001.06453v1</id>
    <title>Action Complexity for Semi-Classical Black Holes</title>
    <updated>2020-01-17T17:53:43Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2001.06453v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2001.06453v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>We adapt the complexity as action prescription (CA) to a semi-classical model of two-dimensional dilaton gravity and determine the rate of increase of holographic complexity for an evaporating black hole. The results are consistent with our previous numerical results for semi-classical black hole complexity using a volume prescription (CV) in the same model, but the CA calculation is fully analytic and provides a non-trivial positive test for the holographic representation of the black hole interior.</summary>
